  "one_candidate": {
    "mechanism": "Guardian underwater sky projection gates all but the explicit one-in-twenty exposure exception while water and difficulty remain matched.",
    "native_flow": [
      "Base monument structure provides a full-bounds MONSTER override with regular Guardian 1 weight, nominal size 2–4. ChunkGenerator replaces the biome list when a qualifying override is found. Forge PotentialSpawns receives and can alter or cancel that result before native selection and recheck. No Guardian or Elder Guardian row was found in the checked raw base biome JSON.",
      "Guardian applies IN_WATER physical placement before the registered NATURAL callback. The physical check requires center water and a non-conductive block above. The predicate draws nextInt(20) first; only a zero draw skips the sky helper. It then requires non-Peaceful and water below and center for the NATURAL reason. The center SPAWNER alternative belongs to a separate reason and is excluded.",
      "At or above sea level the helper uses sky light at the candidate. Below sea level it first asks for sky at the same X/Z at sea level. It then scans strictly above candidate Y, and positive light-blocking material matters only when the block state is not liquid. Fluid opacity alone is not the decisive criterion in this scan.",
      "With default listeners, fixed valid point and all other callback constraints true, a sky-visible point passes 1/20 draws and a sky-hidden point passes all 20/20. These are per callback branch counts. Cumulative spawn rate, effective structure table, admission and survival require their own evidence. Guardian body obstruction uses isUnobstructed without generic containsAnyLiquid veto.",
      "Elder Guardian shares the registered callback if selected on that route. The monument Elder piece code instead directly constructs the separate entity and uses STRUCTURE finalization; do not infer a NATURAL birth from that sighting."
    ],
